From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:19:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DemuxStreamSSIF: a 3D picture keeps the time it was read at

The time Kodi shows for a disc played with its menus is the time each
packet was read at, carried to the picture it belongs to. A 3D
picture is its base view and its second view merged into a new packet,
and the merge kept the timestamps but not that time: no 3D picture
carried it. The shown time went by the read position, tens of seconds
ahead of the picture, and while the player played out a clip before
the next one - a disc's trailers, joined without a seamless connection
- it stood still for as long as the play-out lasted.

The merged packet now keeps the base view's read time, as a 2D packet
does.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
index 52e8035d..597a1911 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
@@ -203,6 +203,7 @@ DemuxPacket* CDemuxStreamSSIF::MergePacket(DemuxPacket* &srcPkt, DemuxPacket* &a
   newpkt->pts = srcPkt->pts;
   newpkt->dts = srcPkt->dts;
   newpkt->duration = srcPkt->duration;
+  newpkt->dispTime = srcPkt->dispTime;
   newpkt->iGroupId = srcPkt->iGroupId;
   newpkt->iStreamId = srcPkt->iStreamId;
   memcpy(newpkt->pData, srcPkt->pData, srcPkt->iSize);
